[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: tracking module (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSeparate tracking.js owns sessionStorage; login() returns userId; the handler wires them. Clear seam, testable, [39m
     [38;5;246mone-line swap to localStorage.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: login() stores it
     [38;5;246mFewer call-site changes, but login() becomes side-effecting and harder to test. Every future caller writes storage
[39m     [38;5;246mimplicitly.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: event bus
     [38;5;246mlogin() emits, a tracker subscribes. Most extensible, most indirection. Worth it only if many other forms will emit
